---

## 8. Apply the Remaining Stash

I checked:

```bash
git stash list
```

There was one stash remaining:

```text
stash@{0}: WIP on feature-profile: 35fe775 file
```

I ran:

```bash
git stash pop stash@{0}
```

Git reported:

```text
error: Your local changes to the following files would be overwritten by merge:
    vim.txt
```

The stash was kept:

```text
The stash entry is kept in case you need it again.
```

### `git stash pop` vs `git stash apply`

| Command           | Behavior                                                 |
| ----------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |
| `git stash pop`   | Applies the stash and removes it if successfully applied |
| `git stash apply` | Applies the stash but keeps it in the stash list         |

### When Would I Use Stash?

I would use stash when I have unfinished work and need to temporarily switch branches for another task.

For example:

```text
Working on feature
       ↓
Urgent production fix
       ↓
git stash
       ↓
Switch to hotfix branch
       ↓
Fix production issue
       ↓
Return to feature
       ↓
git stash pop
```

